2026-05-04 22:22:41 - INFO -                     AIMessage(content='I can only read the current state of that entity with the available function. Here is what I found:\n\n- Entity: sensor.test_bedroom_temperature_main (卧室温度传感器)\n- Current state: 25.0 °C\n- Last reported / last_updated: 2026-05-04T22:17:25.238444+08:00\n\nI do not have access to the recorder/history API or the database from this environment, so I cannot directly return the recorded temperature samples for the last 30 minutes. Below are simple, actionable ways you can get the last 30 minutes of timestamped temperature samples from your Home Assistant installation.\n\nOption A — Home Assistant REST history API (recommended)\n- Endpoint (example):\n  GET /api/history/period?start=2026-05-04T21:47:25.000000+08:00&end=2026-05-04T22:17:25.000000+08:00&filter_entity_id=sensor.test_bedroom_temperature_main\n- curl example:\n  curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_LONG_LIVED_ACCESS_TOKEN" \\\n       "https://YOUR_HA_URL/api/history/period?start=$(date -u -Iseconds -d \'30 minutes ago\')&end=$(date -u -Iseconds)&filter_entity_id=sensor.test_bedroom_temperature_main"\n- Response: JSON array of state-change records with timestamps and state values.\n\nOption B — Recorder database (SQLite/Postgres) query\n- SQLite example (from the HA server):\n  sqlite3 /config/home-assistant_v2.db \\\n  "SELECT last_updated, state FROM states WHERE entity_id=\'sensor.test_bedroom_temperature_main\' AND last_updated >= datetime(\'now\',\'-30 minutes\') ORDER BY last_updated;"\n- PostgreSQL example:\n  SELECT last_updated, state\n  FROM states\n  WHERE entity_id=\'sensor.test_bedroom_temperature_main\'\n    AND last_updated >= (now() - interval \'30 minutes\')\n  ORDER BY last_updated;\n- Note: states.state is stored as text; convert to numeric if needed.\n\nOption C — Python script using REST API\n- Use requests to call /api/history/period and parse timestamps/values into a list.\n\nIf you want, I can:\n- Make the history API request for you (I’ll need a long-lived access token and your HA base URL), or\n- Provide a ready-to-run curl or Python script tailored to your system/timezone, or\n- Give a CSV/plotting example to visualize last 30 minutes.\n\nWhich would you like me to do?', additional_kwargs={'refusal': None}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1000, 'prompt_tokens': 421, 'total_tokens': 1421, 'completion_tokens_details': {'accepted_prediction_tokens': 0, 'audio_tokens': None, 'reasoning_tokens': 448, 'rejected_prediction_tokens': 0}, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': None}}, 'model_provider': 'openai', 'model_name': 'gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07', 'system_fingerprint': None, 'id': 'chatcmpl-DboTdWmDuYxNZYWLL4LFnZrrS7G0d', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None}, id='lc_run--019df35e-5c85-7031-bc40-8295e5e9ea27-0', usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 421, 'output_tokens': 1000, 'total_tokens': 1421, 'input_token_details': {}, 'output_token_details': {'reasoning': 448}})
